bt  but there is actually some reason that  is  in injecting itself  embedding itself in the brains of some  committed right-wingers but we can't  forgive the ignorance if our population  had been  better at critical thinking and had done  10 minutes of actual research back in  2016  trump never would have been the nominee  and certainly never would have become  president of the united states many of  the unnecessary coronavirus deaths that  we've had  would would not have happened and that  number is likely to hit 160 000 in the  next day or two so what we want to do  here is understand what's happening so  that it doesn't happen again  starting with this november but we can't  forget how it happened  we can't ignore that it could happen  again and it still might happen again  in november if we don't vote so to go  back to georgia for a moment  it's not just that there's a margin of  error and trump might actually be  winning like that's one one  interpretation would be  okay biden's plus one but you look at  the margin of error  could really be trump plus six that's  that's one part of it  the other part of it is when you look at  the history of voter suppression in  georgia  when you look at the planned voter  suppression in georgia  it should give us zero confidence that  these close  states are even going to have a shot at  going our way  unless we completely overwhelm the  voting  in november so it's a sad reality  there's a lot we're up against right now  and it includes  five or six different ways in which  donald trump is going to try to suppress  the vote we have to accept it and work  with it and what that means is  so overwhelming voting turnout and every  every election both sides say it we're  our side's motivated we're going to have  record turnout and very often  particularly among some voting groups it  doesn't  happen we actually have to do that to  overwhelm  trump kneecapping the post office voter  purges  limiting vote by mail and on and on and 